<title>INDIA: India approves Air Liquide unit's plan.</title>
<headline>India approves Air Liquide unit's plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian Industry Ministry said on Friday it approved a plan by a unit of France's Air Liquide to set up a wholly-owned gas subsidiary.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the value of proposed foreign direct investment in Air Liquide Holding India Pvt Ltd's project was 1.0 billion rupees.  </p>
<p>The statement said the Indian unit would set up a &quot;wholly-owned subsidiary for manufacture and distribution of industrial, medical and other high purity rare gases&quot;.</p>
<p>- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
